    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "No. 16 Sidney Place is ideally located on the historic Welllington Road, just a stone throw from the newly rejuvenated MacCurtain Street and the St. Luke’s area.  A number of popular bars and restaurants are at your doorstep and the property is just a 6 minute walk from Kent Train Station bus station. \r\nOriginally constructed circa 1820s a dormer was later added to improve the internal space on the top floor. Thompsons Bakery would have been the landmark of the area at the time and it is likely that the houses at Sidney Place were constructed for artisan workers. \r\nThe property is set back off the road with a terrace to the front and a spacious garden to the rear. There is on street parking available all along Wellington Road. \r\nWhile in need of refurbishment, 16 Sidney Place offers ample accommodation set over 4 floors including a basement level. With period features throughout, the property provides an excellent opportunity to restore an historic piece of architecture in the heart of Cork City.  \r\nAccommodation:\r\nGround floor: Kitchen, Dining Room, Storage Room, Utility And Hall\r\nFirst floor: Living Room and Bathroom\r\nSecond floor: 2 bedrooms \r\nThird floor: 1 Bedroom\r\nBasement level: Bathroom\r\n\r\nServices:\r\nMains water and sewer.\r\n\r\nBER: E No. 114717549"
      },
